  "issue_title": "Fails to trigger when expression karatesized ... ehm ... parenthesized",
  "issue_body": "### Before submitting\n\n- [x] I have searched the existing issues and this hasn't been reported yet.\n- [x] I am running the latest stable version of RuboCop.\n\n### Issue type\n\nFalse negative\n\n### Cop name\n\nStyle/SelfAssignment\n\n### Steps to reproduce the problem\n\n```ruby\na = 0\na = a | 1\na = (a | 2)\nputs a\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`Use self-assignment shorthand` should trigger for `a = (a | 2)` too.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nTriggers only for `a = a | 1`\n\n### RuboCop configuration\n\n```yaml\n/dev/null\n```\n\n### RuboCop version\n\n```shell\nSystem Version: macOS 27.0 (26A428)\nModel Identifier: MacBookAir10,1\nruby 4.0.7 (2026-09-15 revision 229531a6cf) +PRISM [arm64-darwin25]\nrubocop     2026-10-01 18d6b7bd1\n```",
